There are many ways to center a div in CSS, each suitable for different layout contexts. Here is a comprehensive overview of all major techniques with code examples.

**1. Flexbox (modern, most versatile):**
```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;  /* horizontal */
  align-items: center;      /* vertical */
}
```

**2. Grid (equally modern and powerful):**
```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;  /* shorthand for both axes */
}
/* Alternative */
.parent {
  display: grid;
  justify-items: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

**3. Margin auto (horizontal centering only, requires fixed width):**
```css
.child {
  width: 300px;
  margin: 0 auto;  /* left and right auto margins */
}
```

**4. Absolute positioning with transform (works when parent has relative positioning):**
```css
.parent {
  position: relative;
}
.child {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

**5. Absolute positioning with margin auto (requires explicit width/height on child):**
```css
.parent {
  position: relative;
}
.child {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0;
  width: 200px;
  height: 100px;
  margin: auto;
}
```

**6. Text-align and line-height (for inline/inline-block elements):**
```css
.parent {
  text-align: center;         /* horizontal */
  line-height: 400px;         /* vertical, must equal parent height */
}
.child {
  display: inline-block;
  vertical-align: middle;
  line-height: normal;
}
```

**7. Table-cell method (older, still works):**
```css
.parent {
  display: table-cell;
  text-align: center;
  vertical-align: middle;
  width: 500px;
  height: 400px;
}
.child {
  display: inline-block;
}
```

**8. CSS Grid with auto margins:**
```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
}
.child {
  margin: auto;  /* centers on both axes */
}
```

**9. Flexbox with auto margin on child:**
```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
}
.child {
  margin: auto;  /* perfect centering on both axes */
}
```

**10. Centering with flow (CSS writing-mode/text-align):**
```css
.parent {
  direction: ltr;
  text-align: center;
}
```

For vertical centering of text, the old-school approach uses `line-height` equal to the container height. For full-page centering, set `html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; }` and apply flexbox or grid to the body. The most recommended modern approach is flexbox for single-axis centering and CSS grid with `place-items: center` for two-axis centering. Always consider the parent's display context and the child's dimensions when choosing a method. Flexbox and grid are widely supported across all modern browsers and handle responsive layouts most gracefully.
